Automation plays as drawn, and one-point curves hold (Segno ADR 0028).

- AutomationIterator (playback) bends a segment with the curve value as given, while
  AutomationCurve::getValueAt and getBezierPoint (drawing, queries) double it; playback now
  doubles it too, so what plays is what's drawn.
- A curve with a single point is treated as empty and never plays; it now holds its value.
- Moving a parameter whose curve has one point moved that point; the DAW decides what a move
  does to automation instead (docs/design/automation.md §7).

